# Full suite before changes

Before editing this repo, run the integration tests and wait for them to
pass. Do not start the change until they are green (or you have recorded a
baseline failure you are about to fix).

```sh
go test -tags=integration -timeout 15m ./test/integration/
```

That builds `gt`, drives the real binary in throwaway repos with a bare
git remote, and never prompts. Stdin is closed. No TTY pickers, no
browser, no `gt-sandbox`.

After the change, run the same command again. A change is not done until
the second run is green.

Do not substitute `go test ./...` (that skips the `integration` tag) or a
single `-run` for this gate. GitHub-only submit/merge/get/pr tests stay
skipped unless `GT_TEST_GITHUB=1`.
